 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:779(phrase)
 msgid "File Format"
@@ -975,21 +1353,32 @@
 msgid ""
 "A file format or file type is the form in which computer data is stored. "
 "Since a file is stored by an operating system as a linear series of bytes, "
-"which cannot describe many kinds of real data in an obvious way, conventions "
-"have been developed for interpreting the information as representations of "
-"complex data. All of the conventions for a particular <quote>kind</quote> of "
-"file constitute a file format."
-msgstr ""
+"which cannot describe many kinds of real data in an obvious way, conventions"
+" have been developed for interpreting the information as representations of "
+"complex data. All of the conventions for a particular <quote>kind</quote> of"
+" file constitute a file format."
+msgstr ""
+"Ett filformat eller en filtyp är den form som datorinformation lagras i. "
+"Eftersom ett operativsystem lagrar en fil som en linjär följd av byte, "
+"vilket inte på ett uppenbart sätt kan beskriva många slags verkliga data, "
+"har konventioner utvecklats för att tolka informationen som representationer"
+" av komplexa data. Alla konventioner för en viss <quote>typ</quote> av fil "
+"utgör ett filformat."
 
