 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2602(para)
 msgid ""
 "YCbCr is a <link linkend=\"glossary-colormodel\">color model</link> which "
 "was developed for the PAL television standard as a simple modification to "
 "the YUV color model. In the meantime, it has become the CCIR-601 standard "
-"for image and video recording. For example, it is used for JPEG pictures and "
-"MPEG videos, and therefore also on DVDs, video CDs and for most other "
+"for image and video recording. For example, it is used for JPEG pictures and"
+" MPEG videos, and therefore also on DVDs, video CDs and for most other "
 "widespread digital video standards. Note that a color model is still not a "
 "color space, since it doesn't determine which colors are actually meant by "
 "<quote>red</quote>, <quote>green</quote> and <quote>blue</quote>. For a "
 "color space, there must still be a reference to a specific absolute color "
 "value."
 msgstr ""
+"YCbCr är en <link linkend=\"glossary-colormodel\">färgmodell</link> som "
+"utvecklades för PAL-tv-standarden som en enkel modifiering av YUV-"
+"färgmodellen. Den har under tiden blivit CCIR-601-standarden för bild- och "
+"videoinspelning. Den används exempelvis för JPEG-bilder och MPEG-video och "
+"därmed även på dvd:er, video-cd:er och de flesta andra utbredda digitala "
+"videostandarder. Observera att en färgmodell fortfarande inte är en färgrymd"
+" eftersom den inte avgör vilka färger som faktiskt avses med "
+"<quote>röd</quote>, <quote>grön</quote> och <quote>blå</quote>. För en "
+"färgrymd krävs fortfarande en hänvisning till ett specifikt absolut "
+"färgvärde."
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2615(para)
 msgid ""
 "There are color models which do not express a color by the additive basic "
-"colors, red, green and blue (RGB), but by other properties, for example, the "
-"brightness-color model. Here, the criteria are the basic brightness of the "
+"colors, red, green and blue (RGB), but by other properties, for example, the"
+" brightness-color model. Here, the criteria are the basic brightness of the "
 "colors (from black, through gray, to white), the colors with the largest "
-"portion (red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet, or other pure colors that "
-"lie between them) and the saturation of the colors (<quote>gaudy</quote> to "
-"pale). This color model is based on the ability of the eye to recognize "
+"portion (red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet, or other pure colors that"
+" lie between them) and the saturation of the colors (<quote>gaudy</quote> to"
+" pale). This color model is based on the ability of the eye to recognize "
 "small differences in luminosity better than small color differences, and to "
-"recognize those better than small differences in saturation. That makes gray "
-"text written on a black background easy to read, but blue text on a red "
+"recognize those better than small differences in saturation. That makes gray"
+" text written on a black background easy to read, but blue text on a red "
 "background very hard to read, even with the same basic brightness. Such "
 "color models are called brightness-color models."
 msgstr ""
+"Det finns färgmodeller som inte uttrycker en färg med de additiva "
+"grundfärgerna rött, grönt och blått (RGB), utan genom andra egenskaper, "
+"exempelvis ljushetsfärgmodellen. Kriterierna är färgernas grundläggande "
+"ljushet (från svart via grått till vitt), färgen med störst andel (rött, "
+"orange, gult, grönt, blått, violett eller andra rena färger däremellan) samt"
+" färgernas mättnad (från <quote>gräll</quote> till blek). Färgmodellen "
+"bygger på ögats förmåga att känna igen små skillnader i luminositet bättre "
+"än små färgskillnader, och dessa bättre än små skillnader i mättnad. Därför "
+"är grå text mot svart bakgrund lätt att läsa, medan blå text mot röd "
+"bakgrund är mycket svår att läsa, även med samma grundläggande ljushet. "
+"Sådana färgmodeller kallas ljushetsfärgmodeller."
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2631(para)
+#| msgid ""
+#| "The YCbCr model is a slight adaptation of such a brightness-color model. An "
+#| "RBG color value is divided into a basic brightness, Y, and two components, "
+#| "Cb and Cr, where Cb is a measurement of the deviation from gray in the blue "
+#| "direction, or if it is less that 0.5, in the direction of yellow. Cr is the "
+#| "corresponding measurement for the difference in the direction of red or "
+#| "turquoise. This representation uses the peculiarity of the eye of being "
+#| "especially sensitive to green light. That is why most of the information "
+#| "about the proportion of green is in the basic brightness, Y, an only the "
+#| "deviations for the red and blue portions need to be represented. The Y "
+#| "values have twice the resolution of the other two values, Cb and Cr, in most"
+#| " practical applications, such as on DVDs."
 msgid ""
 "The YCbCr model is a slight adaptation of such a brightness-color model. An "
 "RGB color value is divided into a basic brightness, Y, and two components, "
@@ -2631,36 +3889,78 @@
 "especially sensitive to green light. That is why most of the information "
 "about the proportion of green is in the basic brightness, Y, and only the "
 "deviations for the red and blue portions need to be represented. The Y "
-"values have twice the resolution of the other two values, Cb and Cr, in most "
-"practical applications, such as on DVDs."
+"values have twice the resolution of the other two values, Cb and Cr, in most"
+" practical applications, such as on DVDs."
 msgstr ""
+"YCbCr-modellen är en mindre anpassning av en modell som beskriver ljushet "
+"och färg. Ett RGB-färgvärde delas upp i en grundläggande ljushet, Y, och två"
+" komponenter, Cb och Cr. Cb mäter avvikelsen från grått i blå riktning "
+"eller, om värdet är lägre än 0,5, i gul riktning. Cr mäter motsvarande "
+"avvikelse i röd eller turkos riktning. Representationen utnyttjar att ögat "
+"är särskilt känsligt för grönt ljus. Därför finns större delen av "
+"informationen om andelen grönt i grundljusheten Y, medan endast avvikelserna"
+" för rött och blått behöver representeras. I de flesta praktiska "
+"tillämpningar, till exempel på dvd:er, har Y-värdena dubbelt så hög "
+"upplösning som Cb- och Cr-värdena."
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2656(para)
-msgid ""
-"YUV is a <link linkend=\"glossary-colormodel\">color model</link> which uses "
-"two components to represent the color information, luma (the strength of the "
-"light per area) and the chrominance, or proportion of color (chroma), where "
-"the chrominance again consists of two components. The development of the YUV "
-"color model also goes back to the development of color television (PAL), "
-"where ways were sought for transmitting the color information along with the "
-"black-and-white signal, in order to achieve backwards compatibility with old "
-"black and white televisions without having to increase the available "
-"transmission bandwidth. From the YUV color model of the analog television "
-"techniques, the YCrCb color model was developed, which is used for most "
-"kinds of digital image and video compression. Erroneously, the YUV color "
-"model is also often spoken about in those fields, although the YCbCr model "
-"is actually used. This often causes confusion."
-msgstr ""
+#| msgid ""
+#| "YUV is a <link linkend=\"glossary-colormodel\">color model</link> which uses"
+#| " two components to represent the color information, luma (the strength of "
+#| "the light per area) and the chrominance, or proportion of color (chroma), "
+#| "where the chrominance again consists of two components. The development of "
+#| "the YUV color model also goes back to the development of color television "
+#| "(PAL), where ways were sought for transmitting the color information along "
+#| "with the black-and-white signal, in order to achieve backwards compatibility"
+#| " with old black and white televisions without having to increase the "
+#| "available transmission bandwidth. From the YUV color model of the analog "
+#| "television techiques, the YCrCb color model was developed, which is used for"
+#| " most kinds of digital image and video compression. Erroneously, the YUV "
+#| "color model is also often spoken about in those fields, although the YCbCr "
+#| "model is actually used. This often causes confusion."
+msgid ""
+"YUV is a <link linkend=\"glossary-colormodel\">color model</link> which uses"
+" two components to represent the color information, luma (the strength of "
+"the light per area) and the chrominance, or proportion of color (chroma), "
+"where the chrominance again consists of two components. The development of "
+"the YUV color model also goes back to the development of color television "
+"(PAL), where ways were sought for transmitting the color information along "
+"with the black-and-white signal, in order to achieve backwards compatibility"
+" with old black and white televisions without having to increase the "
+"available transmission bandwidth. From the YUV color model of the analog "
+"television techniques, the YCrCb color model was developed, which is used "
+"for most kinds of digital image and video compression. Erroneously, the YUV "
+"color model is also often spoken about in those fields, although the YCbCr "
+"model is actually used. This often causes confusion."
+msgstr ""
+"YUV är en <link linkend=\"glossary-colormodel\">färgmodell</link> som "
+"använder två komponenter för att representera färginformationen: luma "
+"(ljusets styrka per ytenhet) och krominans, eller färgandelen (kroma), där "
+"krominansen i sin tur består av två komponenter. Utvecklingen av "
+"färgmodellen YUV går tillbaka till färgtelevisionens utveckling (PAL), då "
+"man sökte sätt att sända färginformationen tillsammans med den svartvita "
+"signalen för att få bakåtkompatibilitet med äldre svartvita tv-apparater "
+"utan att öka den tillgängliga överföringsbandbredden. Ur den analoga tv-"
+"teknikens YUV-färgmodell utvecklades färgmodellen YCrCb, som används för de "
+"flesta typer av digital bild- och videokomprimering. Felaktigt talar man "
+"också ofta om färgmodellen YUV på dessa områden, trots att det egentligen är"
+" modellen YCbCr som används. Detta orsakar ofta förvirring."
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2673(para)
 msgid ""
 "For the calculation of the luma signals, the underlying RGB data is first "
-"adjusted with the <link linkend=\"glossary-gamma\">gamma</link> value of the "
-"output device, and an R'G'B' signal is obtained. The three individual "
-"components are added together with different weights, to form the brightness "
-"information, which also functions as the VBS signal (Video Baseband Signal, "
-"the black-and-white signal) for the old black and white televisions."
-msgstr ""
+"adjusted with the <link linkend=\"glossary-gamma\">gamma</link> value of the"
+" output device, and an R'G'B' signal is obtained. The three individual "
+"components are added together with different weights, to form the brightness"
+" information, which also functions as the VBS signal (Video Baseband Signal,"
+" the black-and-white signal) for the old black and white televisions."
+msgstr ""
+"Vid beräkning av lumasignaler justeras underliggande RGB-data först med "
+"utmatningsenhetens <link linkend=\"glossary-gamma\">gammavärde</link>, och "
+"en R'G'B'-signal erhålls. De tre enskilda komponenterna adderas med olika "
+"vikter för att bilda ljushetsinformationen, som också fungerar som VBS-"
+"signalen (Video Baseband Signal, den svartvita signalen) för de gamla "
+"svartvita tv-apparaterna."
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2682(para)
 msgid "Y=R+G+B"
@@ -2670,10 +3970,14 @@
 msgid ""
 "The exact calculation is more complicated, however, since some aspects of "
 "the color perception of the human eye have to be taken into account. For "
-"example, green is perceived to be lighter than red, and this is perceived to "
-"be lighter than blue. Furthermore, in some systems gamma correction of the "
+"example, green is perceived to be lighter than red, and this is perceived to"
+" be lighter than blue. Furthermore, in some systems gamma correction of the "
 "basic color is first performed."
 msgstr ""
+"Den exakta beräkningen är dock mer komplicerad eftersom vissa aspekter av "
+"det mänskliga ögats färguppfattning måste beaktas. Grönt uppfattas "
+"exempelvis som ljusare än rött, och rött som ljusare än blått. I vissa "
+"system utförs dessutom först gammakorrigering av grundfärgen."
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2690(para)
 msgid ""
@@ -2681,6 +3985,9 @@
 "color information. They are formed by the difference of blue minus luma or "
 "red minus luma."
 msgstr ""
+"Krominanssignalerna, och även färgdifferenssignalerna, innehåller "
+"färginformationen. De bildas av skillnaden mellan blått och luma respektive "
+"rött och luma."
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2695(para)
 msgid "U=B-Y"
@@ -2695,6 +4002,8 @@
 "From the three generated components, Y, U and V, the individual color "
 "proportions of the basic color can be calculated again later:"
 msgstr ""
+"Från de tre skapade komponenterna Y, U och V kan grundfärgens enskilda "
+"färgandelar senare beräknas på nytt:"
 
 #: src/glossary/glossary.xml:2701(para)
 msgid "Y + U = Y + ( B - Y ) = Y - Y + B = B"
@@ -2712,9 +4021,13 @@
 msgid ""
 "Furthermore, because of the structure of the retina of the human eye, it "
 "turns out that the brightness information is perceived at a higher "
-"resolution than the color, so that many formats based on the YUV color model "
-"compress the chrominance to save bandwidth during transmission."
+"resolution than the color, so that many formats based on the YUV color model"
+" compress the chrominance to save bandwidth during transmission."
 msgstr ""
+"På grund av hur människans näthinna är uppbyggd uppfattas "
+"ljushetsinformationen med högre upplösning än färgen. Därför komprimerar "
+"många format som bygger på YUV-färgmodellen krominansen för att spara "
+"bandbredd vid överföring."
 
 #~ msgid ""
